.TH SDL_GPUTextureTransferInfo 3type "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 DATATYPES"
.SH NAME
SDL_GPUTextureTransferInfo \- A structure specifying parameters related to transferring data to or from a texture.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_gpu.h>
.PP
.BI "typedef struct SDL_GPUTextureTransferInfo
.BI "{
.BI "    SDL_GPUTransferBuffer *transfer_buffer;  /**< The transfer buffer used in the transfer operation. */
.BI "    Uint32 offset;                           /**< The starting byte of the image data in the transfer buffer. */
.BI "    Uint32 pixels_per_row;                   /**< The number of pixels from one row to the next. */
.BI "    Uint32 rows_per_layer;                   /**< The number of rows from one layer/depth-slice to the next. */
.BI "} SDL_GPUTextureTransferInfo;
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If either of
.BR pixels_per_row
or
.BR rows_per_layer
is zero, then width and height of passed
.BR SDL_GPUTextureRegion
to
.BR SDL_UploadToGPUTexture
or
.BR SDL_DownloadFromGPUTexture
are used as default values respectively and data is considered to be tightly packed\[char46]
.PP
.BR WARNING :
On some older/integrated hardware, Direct3D 12 requires texture data row pitch to be 256 byte aligned, and offsets to be aligned to 512 bytes\[char46] If they are not, SDL will make a temporary copy of the data that is properly aligned, but this adds overhead to the transfer process\[char46] Apps can avoid this by aligning their data appropriately, or using a different GPU backend than Direct3D 12\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This struct is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR SDL_UploadToGPUTexture (3),
.BR SDL_DownloadFromGPUTexture (3),
.BR SDL_GPUTransferBuffer (3type)
